    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "NITI Aayog is a non-constitutional and non-statutory body created via executive resolution.",
        "National Human Rights Commission (NHRC) is a statutory body established under the Protection of Human Rights Act, 1993.",
        "Removal of the Comptroller and Auditor General (CAG) requires a process similar to the removal of a Supreme Court Judge."
      ],
      "id": "72tnzr6"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Constitutional bodies derive their powers and authority directly from the Constitution of India.",
        "Statutory bodies are created by an Act passed by the Parliament or State Legislature.",
        "Executive or non-statutory bodies are formed by an executive resolution or cabinet decision.",
        "Any change in the status of a constitutional body requires a constitutional amendment under Article 368."
      ],
